# Four lines pasted at once, and what they cost.
Shot paste
Alt four lines pasted at once — a type, a method, a value and a call — each echoed as if typed, then built and run as one program, with :time showing the one build
Caption Paste a block and it is echoed line by line, then built once: four lines, one compile.
Headline Paste a block, pay for one build
Promo 1:1
Varies
Grid 80x14
Line :time on
Paste <<
type Point struct{ X, Y int }
func (p Point) Dist2() int { return p.X*p.X + p.Y*p.Y }
p := Point{3, 4}
p.Dist2()
>>
Wait Prompt
Screenshot
